                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A projectile.",
                                            "An engine operating similarly to the pyrotechnic, generating thrust by the expulsion of hot gases; a rocket engine."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e582e6e8-2856-3228-a3ee-a56c4985014b",
                                        "entry_id": "b899d65b-42f5-3ba7-a9ae-20ee5f523da0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Figurative uses.",
                                            "Something that travels high in the air and/or with great speed; especially (sport), a hard shot."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "10e961af-95de-4e82-8fc0-08b8a7842be9",
                                                "sense_id": "e582e6e8-2856-3228-a3ee-a56c4985014b",
                                                "text": "Fernandinho launched a rocket that flew just over. Gundogan's shot hit off Sviatchenko and Gordon and went out. City pressed and pressed."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bb7840b8-3978-3516-9aca-46ff80943c4f",
                                        "entry_id": "b899d65b-42f5-3ba7-a9ae-20ee5f523da0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Figurative uses.",
                                            "A severe reprimand; a telling-off."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5bfbcd3f-d3e0-4368-8327-c0fa66edac8b",
                                                "sense_id": "bb7840b8-3978-3516-9aca-46ff80943c4f",
                                                "text": "The Burmese nurse who'd gone with her was crying, for which she'd no doubt get a rocket from matron."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b2642531-6fba-4840-a203-235fbb41ff85",
                                                "sense_id": "bb7840b8-3978-3516-9aca-46ff80943c4f",
                                                "text": "While Solborg and Lemaigre were dreaming of revolts, Donovan had learned of Solborg’s insubordination and meddling. He sent him a “rocket” ordering him out of North Africa and back to Lisbon at once."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ab37e377-988b-3dad-9a2d-86e1c2617290",
                                        "entry_id": "b899d65b-42f5-3ba7-a9ae-20ee5f523da0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Figurative uses.",
                                            "An ace (the playing card)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7f0c22a6-c8e3-3e6c-a638-453a0aaded31",
                                        "entry_id": "b899d65b-42f5-3ba7-a9ae-20ee5f523da0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Figurative uses.",
                                            "A stupid or crazy person."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Scotland",
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "064599a6-74d8-4b3c-8a13-e85dd406159f",
                                                "sense_id": "7f0c22a6-c8e3-3e6c-a638-453a0aaded31",
                                                "text": "Why were the Luddites named efter Ned Ludd? A wee rocket. A wee fucken fairy bampot. A pure hooligan, smashing stuff up. A ned. Ned Ludd."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "53cf0f30-4eb9-3e88-9b38-e0a675d544cb",
                                        "entry_id": "b899d65b-42f5-3ba7-a9ae-20ee5f523da0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Figurative uses.",
                                            "A very physically attractive woman."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "East",
                                            "England",
                                            "South",
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "rocket",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "05dfc801-6de7-33c8-802c-6de6bc5f6f6f",
                                        "entry_id": "ff502a09-f6d8-3200-92fd-edc542deb1e2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To accelerate swiftly and powerfully."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "ambitransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "688ea7db-5262-45d0-bb4d-5ed096d50dc8",
                                                "sense_id": "05dfc801-6de7-33c8-802c-6de6bc5f6f6f",
                                                "text": "With Free Guy, Reynolds gets just a little more in touch with his Carrey side via nothing less than his own version of The Truman Show, shorn of its daydream dread and rocketed into the age of Fortnite."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ece32bb1-3fb1-3c65-94e8-a93549e2b839",
                                        "entry_id": "ff502a09-f6d8-3200-92fd-edc542deb1e2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To fly vertically."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "59936580-60e7-3a8f-9ca8-b42613496879",
                                        "entry_id": "ff502a09-f6d8-3200-92fd-edc542deb1e2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To rise or soar rapidly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "18b26da9-ae63-4ca1-b156-4d040d654bca",
                                                "sense_id": "59936580-60e7-3a8f-9ca8-b42613496879",
                                                "text": "The project was attractive because of the ability to maximise the use of existing and decommissioned railways, minimise land take, and decrease the amount of disruption during the project. With London land prices rocketing, there was also a significant financial incentive."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f624c12d-7844-4065-ad98-675f4b790a9b",
                                                "sense_id": "59936580-60e7-3a8f-9ca8-b42613496879",
                                                "text": "The cost of food in the UK had rocketed by 25% since 2019, the researchers calculated, but if the post-Brexit trade restrictions were not in place then this increase would be only 17% – nearly a third lower."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5ffe539c-113d-322f-86d5-a98aea7bee02",
                                        "entry_id": "ff502a09-f6d8-3200-92fd-edc542deb1e2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To experience sudden fame, popularity, or success."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "77a85697-16be-4eaa-9343-f6575f8aab04",
                                                "sense_id": "5ffe539c-113d-322f-86d5-a98aea7bee02",
                                                "text": "After spending years in obscurity, the band finally rocketed last week."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
